## 1. MVVM Clean Architecture Diagrams

### Layered Architecture Flowchart

The diagram below illustrates how data and control flow between the **UI Layer**, **Domain Layer**, and **Data Layer**.

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph UI_Layer ["1. UI Layer (Presentation)"]
        View["SwiftUI Screen View"]
        VM["MVVM ViewModel (@Observable / @MainActor)"]
        State["ProfileUiState (Enum Contract)"]
    end

    subgraph Domain_Layer ["2. Domain Layer (Pure Business Logic)"]
        UC["Use Cases (e.g. GetUserProfileUseCaseProtocol)"]
        Model["Domain Models (Pure Swift Structs)"]
    end

    subgraph Data_Layer ["3. Data Layer (Single Source of Truth)"]
        Repo["Actor UserProfileRepository"]
        Remote["Remote DataSource (URLSession API)"]
        Local["Local DataSource (Keychain / SwiftData)"]
    end

    %% Flow interactions
    View -- "1. Triggers User Action" --> VM
    VM -- "2. Executes Use Case" --> UC
    UC -- "3. Requests Data" --> Repo
    Repo -- "4a. Fetches Remote API" --> Remote
    Repo -- "4b. Caches in Keychain/SwiftData" --> Local
    Repo -- "5. Returns Domain Model" --> UC
    UC -- "6. Delivers Result" --> VM
    VM -- "7. Updates State Property" --> State
    State -- "8. Recomposes SwiftUI Body" --> View

    %% Styling
    classDef uiStyle fill:#f2fbf5,stroke:#008544,stroke-width:2px;
