### Unidirectional Data Flow (UDF) Sequence Diagram

This sequence diagram illustrates the step-by-step lifecycle of an asynchronous user request using Swift Concurrency.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant View as SwiftUI UserProfileView
    participant VM as UserProfileViewModel (@MainActor)
    participant UC as GetUserProfileUseCase
    participant Repo as UserProfileRepository (Actor)
    participant API as URLSession Network API

    User->>View: Tap "Refresh Profile" Button
    View->>VM: loadUserProfile()
    VM->>VM: Set state = .loading
    View-->>User: Render ProgressView Spinner
    VM->>UC: execute(userId)
    UC->>Repo: fetchProfile(userId)
    Repo->>API: URLSession.shared.data(from: url)
    API-->>Repo: Return Data & HTTPURLResponse
    Repo->>Repo: Decode JSON & Update Actor Memory Cache
    Repo-->>UC: Return UserProfile Struct
    UC-->>VM: Return UserProfile Struct
    VM->>VM: Set state = .success(user)
    VM-->>View: Recompose View Body
    View-->>User: Render Profile Details & Badges
```

